.TH RDW 1 "2025" "rdw" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rdw \- pipe process output into a live browser layout
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rdw
[\fB\-\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR]
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rdw
is a daemon that receives line-oriented output from one or more processes
and displays it in a live multi-pane browser layout.
Panes are identified by a Target ID and updated in real time over WebSocket.
.PP
The server embeds a single-page browser application. No external assets are
needed; the binary is self-contained.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
TCP port to connect to or listen on (default: 7681).
When multiple servers are running use this flag on every command to address
the correct instance.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Server management
.TP
.B rdw server start
Start the rdw server. Options:
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-open\-browser
Open the browser UI immediately after the server starts.
.TP
.B \-\-kv\-persist \fIPATH\fR
Enable SQLite KV persistence at \fIPATH\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-restore
On startup, load the KV store from the SQLite database specified by
\fB\-\-kv\-persist\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-auth
Disable token authentication (development use only).
.RE
.TP
.B rdw server stop
Stop the running server.
.TP
.B rdw server list
List all running rdw server instances.
.SS Piping data
.TP
.B rdw pipe \-\-id \fITARGET_ID\fR
Read from stdin and relay lines to the pane identified by \fITARGET_ID\fR.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-layout \fINAME\fR
Apply the named layout before streaming begins.
.TP
.B \-\-window \fINAME\fR
Route the stream to a specific window.
.TP
.B \-\-forward rd|rdw|both
In addition to rdw, forward stdin to bash-rd (\fBrd\fR), rdw only, or both.
.TP
.B \-\-forward\-to\-file \fIPATH\fR
Mirror the stream to a file or FIFO.
.TP
.B \-\-forward\-to\-cmd \fICMD\fR
Mirror the stream as stdin to a shell command.
.RE
.SS Window management
.TP
.B rdw window create \fINAME\fR
Create a new window.
.TP
.B rdw window close \fINAME\fR
Close a window (blocked if it is the last one).
.TP
.B rdw window rename \fIOLD\fR \fINEW\fR
Rename a window.
.TP
.B rdw window focus \fINAME\fR
Switch the browser view to the named window.
.TP
.B rdw window list
List all windows and their panes.
.SS Pane management
.TP
.B rdw pane split \fIID\fR [\fB\-\-dir h|v\fR]
Split an existing pane horizontally or vertically.
.TP
.B rdw pane resize \fIID\fR \fISIZE\fR
Resize a pane. \fISIZE\fR is \fIN\fR (columns/rows), \fINpx\fR (pixels),
or \fIN%\fR (percentage).
.TP
.B rdw pane zoom \fIID\fR
Toggle zoom on a pane.
.TP
.B rdw pane swap \fIID1\fR \fIID2\fR
Swap the positions of two panes.
.TP
.B rdw pane close \fIID\fR
Remove a pane.
.SS KV store
.TP
.B rdw kv set \fIKEY\fR \fIVALUE\fR
Set a KV entry. Keys follow the pattern
.IR [a-zA-Z0-9_][a-zA-Z0-9_ -]* ,
with an optional \fIwindow:\fR or \fIpane:\fR namespace prefix.
.TP
.B rdw kv get \fIKEY\fR
Print the value of a KV entry.
.TP
.B rdw kv delete \fIKEY\fR
Delete a KV entry.
.TP
.B rdw kv list [\fIPREFIX\fR]
List KV keys, optionally filtered by prefix.
.SS Token management
.TP
.B rdw token create [\fB\-\-scope \fISCOPE\fR] [\fB\-\-expires \fIDURATION\fR]
Create an auth token. The plain-text token is printed once only.
.TP
.B rdw token revoke \fITOKEN_ID\fR
Revoke a token immediately.
.SS Layout management
.TP
.B rdw layout apply \fINAME\fR|\fIPATH\fR
Apply a saved or on-disk layout to the current session.
.TP
.B rdw layout save \fINAME\fR
Snapshot the current layout under \fINAME\fR.
.TP
.B rdw layout list
List saved layouts.
.SS Export
.TP
.B rdw save \fIDIR\fR [\fB\-\-pane \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-window \fINAME\fR]
Export scrollback to a Markdown bundle under \fIDIR\fR. Images are saved as
files in an \fIassets/\fR subdirectory.
.SS Diagnostics
.TP
.B rdw selftest
Run the in-process smoke suite and exit 0 if all checks pass.
.SH CONTROL SEQUENCES
Lines written to
.B rdw pipe
may embed inline control sequences.
All sequences use the form \fIPREFIX\fBkey\fR:\fIvalue\fR.
.TP
.B kv:\fIkey\fR=\fIvalue\fR
Set a KV entry from the stream.
.TP
.B f:\fIformatter\fR
Switch the pane formatter (text, json, yaml, markdown, csv, image).
.TP
.B b64:\fIDATA\fR
Decode base64 data; used with the image formatter.
.TP
.B ts:
Prepend an ISO-8601 timestamp to the following line.
.TP
.B v:\fIDATA\fR
Verbatim passthrough — the remainder of the line is never interpreted as a
control sequence.
.TP
.B hl:\fIPROFILE\fR
Apply the named highlight profile to the pane.
.TP
.B bm:\fINAME\fR
Create a scrollback bookmark at the current line.
.TP
.B sc:\fIACTION\fR
Scrollback control: \fBclear\fR, \fBtop\fR, \fBbottom\fR.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
The server requires a Bearer token on all authenticated endpoints.
Tokens are stored SHA-256 hashed; the plain-text value is shown once at
creation and never again.
.PP
The Unix domain socket at
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/rdw/<session_id>.sock
accepts connections from the local user without a token.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Base directory for the Unix socket. Defaults to \fI/run/user/<uid>\fR.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base directory for the server registry. Defaults to \fI$HOME/.cache\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/rdw/servers.json
Registry of running rdw instances.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/rdw/<id>.sock
Unix socket for the session identified by \fIid\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rd (1)
.SH AUTHORS
rdw was written by nkh. Source: https://github.com/nkh/rdw
